<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-19491] add "nodemap new" alias for "nodemap add"</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19491</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;I think it is a bit confusing to have "&lt;tt&gt;lctl nodemap add&lt;/tt&gt;" create a new nodemap, and then "&lt;tt&gt;nodemap add_range&lt;/tt&gt;" and "&lt;tt&gt;nodemap add_offset&lt;/tt&gt;" to modify the nodemap.  For OST Pools, the commands are "&lt;tt&gt;lctl pool new&lt;/tt&gt;" and "&lt;tt&gt;lctl pool add&lt;/tt&gt;", which gives a better distinction between the two operations IMHO.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think it would be useful to add an alias "&lt;tt&gt;nodemap new&lt;/tt&gt;" that is equivalent to "&lt;tt&gt;nodemap add&lt;/tt&gt;" and start documenting this as the preferred command (keeping "&lt;tt&gt;nodemap add&lt;/tt&gt;" for compatibility.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
